More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (811–820)
811. Improper Validation of API Bulk Operations
Bulk Operation Authorization Bypass
Attackers perform bulk actions like deleting or editing multiple records without proper permission checks.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
812. Insecure Handling of Application Feature Flags
Feature Flag Exposure
Feature flags reveal hidden or experimental features that can be abused.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
813. Improper Validation of Resource Ownership
Resource Ownership Bypass
Applications fail to verify ownership before allowing users to access or modify resources.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
814. Insecure Handling of Scheduled Backup APIs
Scheduled Backup Data Exposure
Backup APIs allow unauthorized access to backup data.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
815. Improper Validation of Group Membership APIs
Group Membership Manipulation
Attackers add or remove users from groups without proper authorization.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
816. Insecure Handling of Authentication Logs
Authentication Log Exposure
Authentication logs expose sensitive user login information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $5,000
817. Improper Validation of Media Access Tokens
Media Access Token Reuse
Media access tokens can be reused to view restricted content.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
818. Insecure Handling of System Configuration APIs
System Configuration API Exposure
Configuration APIs reveal internal application settings.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
819. Improper Validation of Notification Delivery Settings
Notification Delivery Authorization Bypass
Attackers manipulate how notifications are delivered to other users.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
820. Insecure Handling of Cloud Environment Variables
Environment Variable Exposure
Cloud environments expose secrets through environment variables.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
